1=10 (carry 1)\n\nHundred thousands:1 +5 +1=7\n\nMillions:4 +3=7\n\nTen millions:2 +0=2\n\nHundred millions:8 +2=10. Oh right, so here the hundred millions place adds to 10, which would mean we have a 0 in the hundred millions and carry over 1 to the billions place. But since there are no higher digits, that carried 1 becomes a new digit in the billions place. So the total would be 1,027,704,813?\n\nWait, let me do the addition step by step again carefully.\n\nLet me write each number with commas for clarity:\n\nFirst number: 824,190,622\n\nSecond number: 203,514,191\n\nAdding them:\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n        824,190,622\n      + 203,514,191\n      --------------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 2 +1 =3\n\nTens:2 +9=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n\nHundreds:6 +1=7 plus the 1 carried \u2192 8\n\nThousands:0 +4=4\n\nTen thousands:9 +1=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands:1 +5=6 plus 1 \u21927\n\nMillions:4 +3=7\n\nTen millions:2 +0=2\n\nHundred millions:8 +2=10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carried over 1 goes to the next (billions) place. So the total becomes 1,027,704,813?\n\nWait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n824,190,622 + 203,514,191.\n\nLet me add 824,190,622 + 200,000,000 = 1,024,190,622\n\nThen add the remaining 3,514,191:\n\n1,024,190,622 + 3,514,191 = ?\n\nAdding 1,024,190,622 + 3,000,000 = 1,027,190,622\n\nThen add 514,191:\n\n1,027,190,622 + 514,191 = ?\n\nAdding 500,000: 1,027,690,622\n\nThen 14,191: 1,027,690,622 +14,191 = 1,027,704,813. \n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer should be 1,027,704,813. Let me confirm once more with digit-wise addition.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I made a mistake in the initial digit-by-digit steps. Let me go through each digit again step by step:\n\nStarting from the right (ones place):\n\nPosition 1 (ones): 2 +1 =3 \u2192 3\n\nPosition 2 (tens): 2 +9 =11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n\nPosition 3 (hundreds):6 +1 =7 +1 (carry) =8 \u2192 8\n\nPosition4 (thousands):0 +4 =4 \u21924\n\nPosition5 (ten thousands):9 +1 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover1\n\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):1 +5 =6 +1 (carry)=7 \u21927\n\nPosition7 (millions):4 +3 =7 \u21927\n\nPosition8 (ten millions):2 +0 =2 \u21922\n\nPosition9 (hundred millions):8 +2 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover1\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 is added as a new digit to the left, making it 1 followed by the rest. So the total is 1,027,704,813. \n\nYes, that's correct. So the answer is 1,027,704,813.\n</think>\n\n",
