 over 1 makes 12. So here, we write down 2 and carryover 1.\n\nNow, since there are no more digits, the carryover 1 must be added as a new digit to the left. So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we have so far.\n\nPutting all digits together from highest to lowest:\n\nThe digits from position8 (after adding) gave us 2, but with a carryover 1. So the digits are:\n\nCarryover 1, then the result of position8 (2), then position7 (1), then the rest:\n\nSo the digits from left to right would be:\n\n1 (carryover), 2 (position8), 1 (position7), 6 (position6), 5 (position5), 8 (position4), 2 (position3), 6 (position2), 8 (position1), 3 (position0).\n\nWait, let me list them in order:\n\nStarting from the highest place (billions now because of the carryover):\n\nBillions place: 1\n\nThen hundred millions: 2\n\nTen millions:1\n\nMillions:6\n\nHundred thousands:5\n\nTen thousands:8\n\nThousands:2\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:8\n\nUnits:3\n\nSo combining all these digits:\n\n1 (billions), 2 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 3 (units).\n\nSo the number is 1,216,582,683?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let me write the digits in order:\n\nStarting from the highest digit after the carryover:\n\n1 (billions place), then 2 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 6 (millions), 5 (hundred thousands), 8 (ten thousands), 2 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 8 (tens), 3 (units). So the number is 1,216,582,683?\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers directly:\n\n469,180,232\n\n+720,402,451\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 2+1=3\n\nTens:3+5=8\n\nHundreds:2+4=6\n\nThousands:0+2=2\n\nTen thousands:8+0=8\n\nHundred thousands:1+4=5\n\nMillions:6+0=6\n\nTen millions:9+2=11 \u2192 write 1, carryover 1\n\nHundred millions:4+7=11 plus carryover 1 is 12 \u2192 write 2, carryover 1\n\nThen the final carryover 1 becomes the billions place.\