et me recount each step carefully.\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes: 0+5=5 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTens:1+8=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundreds:6+9=15, so 5 with carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nThousands:8+4=12 +1=13 \u2192 3, carryover 1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen thousands:4+9=13 +1=14 \u21924, carryover1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred thousands:1+9=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nMillions:2+3=5 +1=6 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nTen millions:7+8=15 \u21925, carryover1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nHundred millions:3+8=11 +1=12 \u21922, carryover1 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nBillions:0+8=8 +1=9 \u2714\ufe0f\n\nSo the total is 1,256,143,595? Wait, but when I add 372,148,610 and 883,994,985, maybe I should check with another method. Let me add them using another approach.\n\nAlternatively, adding the numbers as whole:\n\n372,148,610\n\n+883,994,985\n\nLet me add the millions first. 372 million plus 883 million is 1,255 million. Then the remaining parts: 148,610 + 994,985. \n\n148,610 + 994,985: \n\n148,610 + 900,000 = 1,048,610\n\nThen add 94,985: 1,048,610 + 94,985 = 1,143,595\n\nSo total is 1,255,000,000 + 1,143,595 = 1,256,143,595. Okay, that matches. So the answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n",
