t) +1 (second) +1 (carryover) =2. Write 2, no carryover.\n\nPosition 7 (ten millions):\n5 (first) +5 (second) =10. Write 0, carryover 1.\n\nPosition 8 (hundred millions):\n7 (first) +6 (second) +1 (carryover) =14. Write 4, carryover 1. But since there are no more digits, we need to add that carryover as a new digit to the left. So the total becomes 1 in the next position (billions place).\n\nPutting all together, starting from the right:\n\nPositions 0-8 digits after addition (with carries):\n\nPosition 0:1\n\nPosition1:1\n\nPosition2:4\n\nPosition3:1\n\nPosition4:5\n\nPosition5:6\n\nPosition6:2\n\nPosition7:0\n\nPosition8:4\n\nPlus the final carryover 1 in the billions place (position9).\n\nSo the digits from right to left (positions 0 to 9) are:\n\n1 (position0), 1 (1), 4 (2), 1 (3),5 (4),6 (5),2 (6),0 (7),4 (8), and 1 (position9).\n\nSo writing the number from left to right (billions down to ones):\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nWait, let me structure this properly. Let's list each digit's place:\n\n- Position9 (billions): 1\n\n- Position8 (hundred millions):4\n\n- Position7 (ten millions):0\n\n- Position6 (millions):2\n\n- Position5 (hundred thousands):6\n\n- Position4 (ten thousands):5\n\n- Position3 (thousands):1\n\n- Position2 (hundreds):4\n\n- Position1 (tens):1\n\n- Position0 (ones):1\n\nSo combining these digits from highest to lowest place:\n\n1 (billions), 4 (hundred millions), 0 (ten millions), 2 (millions), 6 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 1 (thousands), 4 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nTherefore, the number is 1,402,651,411.\n\nWait, let me verify this with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n750,800,466 + 651,850,945.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\nFirst, 750,800,466 + 600,000,000 = 1,350,800,466\n\nThen add 51,850,945 to that:\n\n1,350,800,466 + 51,850,945.\n\nAdding 50,0