nstruct the digits step by step.\n\nLet me list each place's result:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:4\n\nTens:5 (with carry 1)\n\nHundreds:6\n\nThousands:1\n\nTen-thousands:5 (with carry 1)\n\nHundred-thousands:6 (with carry 1)\n\nMillions:4 (with carry 1)\n\nTen-millions:7\n\nHundred-millions:1 (with carryover 1 to billions)\n\nBillions:1 (from the carryover)\n\nSo putting all together from left to right:\n\nBillions place:1\n\nHundred-millions:1\n\nTen-millions:7\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred-thousands:6\n\nTen-thousands:5\n\nThousands:1\n\nHundreds:6\n\nTens:5\n\nOnes:4\n\nWait, that would be 1,174,651,654. Let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n347,891,063 + 826,760,591.\n\nLet me add them step by step:\n\n347,891,063 + 800,000,000 = 1,147,891,063\n\nThen add 26,760,591:\n\n1,147,891,063 + 26,760,591 = ?\n\n1,147,891,063 + 20,000,000 = 1,167,891,063\n\nThen +6,760,591:\n\n1,167,891,063 + 6,000,000 = 1,173,891,063\n\nThen +760,591:\n\n1,173,891,063 + 700,000 = 1,174,591,063\n\nThen +60,591:\n\n1,174,591,063 + 60,000 = 1,174,651,063\n\nThen +591: 1,174,651,063 + 591 = 1,174,651,654.\n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer is 1,174,651,654. I think that's correct. Let me just confirm once more with another approach, maybe breaking down the numbers:\n\n347,891,063 can be written as 300,000,000 + 47,000,000 + 891,063\n\n826,760,591 is 800,000,000 + 26,000,000 + 760,591\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n300M + 800M = 1,100M\n\n47M +26M =73M \u2192 total so far 1,173M\n\nThen the remaining parts: 891,063 +760,591 = ?\n\n891,063 +700,000 =1,591,063\n\n+60,591 \u2192 1,591,063 +60,591 =1,651,654\n\nSo total sum is 1,173,000,000 +1,651,654 =1,174,651,654. Yep, same result. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 347891063 and 826760591?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.  \n1. The ones place: **3 + 1 = 4**  \n2. The tens place: **6 + 9 = 15** (write **5**, carry **1**)  \n3. The hundreds place