 4 (Thousands): 1 + 3 = 4\n\nPosition 5 (Ten thousands): 0 + 9 = 9\n\nPosition 6 (Hundred thousands): 4 + 8 = 12 \u2192 write 2, carryover 1\n\nPosition 7 (Millions): 6 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 7\n\nPosition 8 (Ten millions): 4 + 6 = 10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\nPosition 9 (Hundred millions): 4 +5 +1 (carry) = 10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1? Wait, but there's no higher place here. Wait, hold on. Wait, the hundred millions place is the 9th digit from the right. The first number's hundred millions digit is 4, the second's is 5. Adding them plus the carryover from the ten millions place (which was 1 from the previous step). Wait, let me retrace:\n\nWait, in position 8 (ten millions place), the digits are 4 (from first number) and 6 (from second). So 4+6 =10, so we write 0 and carryover 1 to the next (hundred millions) place.\n\nThen, the hundred millions place digits are 4 (first number) and 5 (second number). Adding those plus the carryover 1: 4+5+1=10. So that gives 0 in the hundred millions place and a carryover of 1 to the next (billions) place. Since there are no more digits, that 1 becomes a new digit at the beginning.\n\nSo putting it all together:\n\nStarting from the right, the digits we have are:\n\nPositions 1-9 (from right to left):\n\nPosition 1:9\n\nPosition2:6 (with carryover 1)\n\nPosition3:5\n\nPosition4:4\n\nPosition5:9\n\nPosition6:2 (carryover 1)\n\nPosition7:7\n\nPosition8:0 (carryover 1)\n\nPosition9:0 (carryover 1 from previous, but adding 4+5+1 gives 10, so actually, the hundred millions place is 0 and carryover 1 to billions.\n\nSo the total sum would be 1 followed by the digits from the hundred millions down. Wait, let me structure this properly.\n\nLet me write the digits step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (ones):\n\nOnes:9\n\nTens:6 (with a carryover)\n\nHundreds:5\n\nThousands:4\n\nTen thousands:9\n\nHundred thousands:2 (with carryover 1 from hundred thousands place addition)\n\nMillions:7\n\nTen millions:0 (with carryover 1)\