g over with correct place values.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes: 0 +7 =7\n\nTens:9+4=13 (3, carry 1)\n\nHundreds:1+2=3 plus carryover 1 \u21924 (no carry)\n\nThousands:7+3=10 (0, carry1)\n\nTen thousands:4+8=12 plus carry1 \u219213 (3, carry1)\n\nHundred thousands:4+5=9 plus carry1 \u219210 (0, carry1)\n\nMillions:0+0=0 plus carry1 \u21921 (no carry)\n\nTen millions:4 (from first number's ten millions place?) Wait, let me clarify:\n\nWait, the first number's digits:\n\nBreaking down 840,447,190:\n\nPositions (from right, starting at 1):\n\n1:0 (ones)\n\n2:9 (tens)\n\n3:1 (hundreds)\n\n4:7 (thousands)\n\n5:4 (ten thousands)\n\n6:4 (hundred thousands)\n\n7:0 (millions)\n\n8:4 (ten millions)\n\n9:8 (hundred millions)\n\nSecond number 320,583,247:\n\n1:7\n\n2:4\n\n3:2 (hundreds)\n\n4:3 (thousands)\n\n5:8 (ten thousands)\n\n6:5 (hundred thousands)\n\n7:0 (millions)\n\n8:2 (ten millions)\n\n9:3 (hundred millions)\n\nSo when adding the ten millions place (position 8):\n\nFirst number has 4, second has 2 \u21924+2=6. Plus any carryover?\n\nWait, let's track each step again carefully:\n\nStarting over step by step:\n\n1. Ones place: 0 +7 =7. Write 7. Carry 0.\n\n2. Tens place:9 +4 =13. Write 3. Carry 1.\n\n3. Hundreds place:1 +2 =3 +1 (carry) =4. Write 4. Carry 0.\n\n4. Thousands place:7 +3 =10. Write 0. Carry 1.\n\n5. Ten thousands place:4 +8 =12 +1 (carry) =13. Write 3. Carry 1.\n\n6. Hundred thousands place:4 +5 =9 +1 (carry) =10. Write 0. Carry 1.\n\n7. Millions place:0 +0 =0 +1 (carry) =1. Write 1. Carry 0.\n\n8. Ten millions place:4 (from first number) +2 (from second) =6. Write 6. Carry 0.\n\n9. Hundred millions place:8 +3 =11. Write 1, and carry over 1 to the next (billions) place.\n\nNow, since there's a carryover of 1 to the billions place, which wasn't present in the original numbers, so we add that as a new digit at the beginning.\n\nPutting all digits together from right to left:\n\nStarting from the ones digit:\n\n7 (ones), 3 (tens),4 (hundreds),0 (thousa