n9 (hundred millions):6 +5 +1=12 (write2, carry1)\n\nNow, since both numbers are 9 digits, the next position (billions) would be the carryover 1. So the total sum is 1 followed by the digits we have: 1 2 6 4 4 7 4 9 8 7? Wait, let me see:\n\nWait, the digits from position9 (hundred millions) gave us 2 with a carryover 1. The carryover 1 becomes the next digit (billions place). So the digits from left to right would be:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:7\n\nWait, that doesn't seem right. Let me list each digit step by step:\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (position1):\n\nPositions:\n\n1 (ones):7\n\n2 (tens):8\n\n3 (hundreds):9\n\n4 (thousands):4 (with carryover 1)\n\n5 (ten thousands):7\n\n6 (hundred thousands):4 (carryover1)\n\n7 (millions):4 (carryover1)\n\n8 (ten millions):6 (carryover1)\n\n9 (hundred millions):2 (carryover1)\n\nThen the final carryover1 is the billions place.\n\nSo the digits from left (billions) to right (ones):\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:2\n\nTen millions:6\n\nMillions:4\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:4\n\nHundreds:9\n\nTens:8\n\nOnes:7\n\nSo putting them together: 1,264,474,987. Wait, let me check with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n677,737,426 + 586,737,561.\n\nLet me add 677,737,426 + 500,000,000 = 1,177,737,426\n\nThen add 86,737,561: 1,177,737,426 + 86,737,561 = ?\n\n1,177,737,426 + 80,000,000 = 1,257,737,426\n\nThen +6,737,561: 1,257,737,426 +6,737,561 = 1,264,474,987. \n\nYes, that matches. So the final answer is 1,264,474,987. I think that's correct. Let me confirm once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, using column addition:\n\n          677,737,426\n        + 586,737,561\n        ----------------\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:6+1=7\n\nTens:2+6=8\n\nHundreds:4+5=9\n\nThousands:7+7=14 (4, carry 1)\n\nTen thousands:3+3 +1=7\n\nHundred thousan