t, every three digits:\n\nThe number is 920,017,699. So:\n\n- The first comma separates millions: 920 (million), then 017 thousand, 699.\n\nWait, actually, standard notation is:\n\nEach comma separates thousands, millions, etc. So:\n\n920,017,699 is 920 million, 17 thousand, 699.\n\nBreaking down digit by digit:\n\nDigit positions (from right, starting at 0):\n\nPosition 0: 9 (ones)\n\n1:9 (tens)\n\n2:6 (hundreds)\n\n3:7 (thousands)\n\n4:1 (ten thousands)\n\n5:0 (hundred thousands)\n\n6:0 (millions)\n\n7:2 (ten millions)\n\n8:9 (hundred millions)\n\nWait, that's better. So the first number's digits from right to left (positions 0-8):\n\nPositions:\n\n0:9\n\n1:9\n\n2:6\n\n3:7\n\n4:1\n\n5:0\n\n6:0\n\n7:2\n\n8:9\n\nSecond number: 570,178,216\n\nBreaking down similarly:\n\n570,178,216 is 570 million, 178 thousand, 216.\n\nDigits from right (position 0):\n\n0:6\n\n1:1 (tens)\n\n2:2 (hundreds)\n\n3:8 (thousands)\n\n4:7 (ten thousands)\n\n5:1 (hundred thousands)\n\n6:0 (millions)\n\n7:7 (ten millions)\n\n8:5 (hundred millions)\n\nSo now, adding each position:\n\nStarting at position 0:\n\n9 +6 =15 \u2192 5, carryover 1\n\nPosition1:9+1=10 +1=11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nPosition2:6+2=8 +1=9 \u21929, no carry\n\nPosition3:7+8=15 \u21925, carryover1\n\nPosition4:1+7=8 +1=9 \u21929, no carry\n\nPosition5:0+1=1 \u21921\n\nPosition6:0+0=0 \u21920\n\nPosition7:2+7=9 \u21929\n\nPosition8:9+5=14 \u21924, carryover1\n\nWait, but position8 is the hundred millions place. After adding 9+5=14, we have to write 4 and carryover 1. But since there are no more digits beyond position8, that carryover becomes a new digit at position9 (billions place). So the total sum would have a 1 in the billions place.\n\nSo putting all together:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nPositions 0-8 digits after addition (with carries):\n\nPosition0:5\n\n1:1\n\n2:9\n\n3:5\n\n4:9\n\n5:1\n\n6:0\n\n7:9\n\n8:4\n\nPlus the carryover 1 at position9.\n\nSo the digits from position0 to 9 are:\n\nPosition9:1\n\nPosition8:4\n\n7:9\n\n6:0\n\n5:1\n\n4:9\n\n3:5\n\n2:9\n\n1:1\n\n0:5\n\nSo writing the number from highest to lowest position:\n\n1 (billion), 4 (hundred millions), 9 (ten millions), 0 (millions), 1 (hundred thousands), 9 (ten thousands), 5 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 5 (ones).\n\nWait, let me structure that properly:\n\nThe digits are:\n\nPosition9:1 \u2192 billions place\n\nPosition8:4 \u2192 hundred millions\n\nPosition7:9 \u2192 ten millions\n\nPosition6:0 \u2192 millions\n\nPosition5:1 \u2192 hundred thousands\n\nPosition4:9 \u2192 ten thousands\n\nPosition3:5 \u2192 thousands\n\nPosition2:9 \u2192 hundreds\n\nPosition1:1 \u2192 tens\n\nPosition0:5 \u2192 ones\n\nSo the number is 1,490,195,915?\n\nWait, let me check:\n\nBreaking down:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:4 \u2192 1,400,000,000\n\nTen millions:9 \u2192 +90,000,000 \u2192 total 1,490,000,000\n\nMillions:0 \u2192 stays\n\nHundred thousands:1 \u2192 +100,000 \u2192 1,490,100,000\n\nTen thousands:9 \u2192 +90,000 \u2192 1,490,190,000\n\nThousands:5 \u2192 +5,000 \u2192 1,490,195,000\n\nHundreds:9 \u2192 +900 \u2192 1,490,195,900\n\nTens:1 \u2192 +10 \u2192 1,490,195,910\n\nOnes:5 \u2192 +5 \u2192 1,490,195,915.\n\nYes, so the total is 1,490,195,915.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n920,017,699 + 570,178,216.\n\nLet me add 920,017,699 + 500,000,000 = 1,420,017,699.\n\nThen add 70,178,216: 1,420,017,699 +70,000,000 =1,490,017,699.\n\nThen add 178,216: 1,490,017,699 +178,216 = ?\n\n1,490,017,699 + 100,000 =1,490,117,699\n\nThen +78,216: 1,490,117,699 +78,216 =1,490,195,915. \n\nYes, that matches. So the answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 920017699 and 570178216?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.  \n1. The ones place: **9 + 6 = 15** \u2192 Write **5**, carry over **1**.  \n2. The tens place: **9 + 1 + 1 (carry) = 11** \u2192 Write **1**, carry over **1**.  \n3. The hundreds place: **6 + 2 + 1 (