 +3 +1=7 \u21927, carry0\nPosition6 (hundred thousands):1 +8=9 \u21929, carry0\nPosition7 (millions):4 +9=13 \u21923, carry1\nPosition8 (ten millions):3 +7 +1=11 \u21921, carry1\nPosition9 (hundred millions):7 +9 +1=17 \u21927, carry1\nPosition10 (billions): carry1 \u21921\n\nSo the digits from right to left are:\n\n0,1,9,3,7,9,3,1,7,1. Wait, but when written left to right, it's 1 (billions), then 7 (hundred millions), 1 (ten millions), 4? Wait, maybe I messed up the positions.\n\nWait, let me write the digits in order:\n\nThe result digits, starting from the right (ones) to the left (billions):\n\nPositions 1-10:\n\nPosition 1: 0\n\n2:1\n\n3:9\n\n4:3\n\n5:7\n\n6:9\n\n7:3\n\n8:1\n\n9:7\n\n10:1\n\nSo when written as a number, starting from the highest position (position10) to the lowest:\n\nPosition10:1, Position9:7, Position8:1, Position7:3, Position6:9, Position5:7, Position4:3, Position3:9, Position2:1, Position1:0.\n\nSo the number is 1 7 1 3 9 7 3 9 1 0. Wait, that would be 1,713,973,910? Wait, let me group them properly.\n\nBreaking into groups:\n\n1,713,973,910. Let me check:\n\n1 (billion), 713 (million), 973 (thousand), 910. Hmm, but let me verify with another method.\n\nAlternatively, adding the two numbers:\n\n734,134,709 + 979,839,201.\n\nLet me add them as:\n\n734,134,709\n\n+979,839,201\n\n= ?\n\nAdding the millions:\n\n700,000,000 + 900,000,000 = 1,600,000,000\n\n34,000,000 + 79,000,000 = 113,000,000 \u2192 total so far 1,713,000,000\n\nThen 134,000 + 839,000 = 973,000 \u2192 total 1,713,973,000\n\nThen 709 + 201 = 910 \u2192 total 1,713,973,910. Okay, that matches. So the answer is 1,713,973,910.\n\nWait, but in my first digit-by-digit approach, I had the same result. So the final answer should be 1,713,973,910. Let me confirm once more with another method.\n\nAlternatively, using calculator-like addition:\n\n734,134,709\n\n+979,839,201\n\nAdding digit by digit again:\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nOnes:9+1=10 \u21920, carry1\n\nTens:0+0+1=1 \u21921, carry0\n\nHundreds:7+2=9 \u21929\n\nThousands:4+9=13 \u21923, carry1\n\nTen thousands:3+3+1=7 \u21927\n\nHundred thousands:1+8=9 \u21929\n\nMillions:4+9=13 \u21923, carry1\n\nTen millions:3+7+1=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nHundred millions:7+9+1=17 \u21927, carry1\n\nBillions:0+0+1=1 \u21921\n\nSo the digits from right to left are 0,1,9,3,7,9,3,1,7,1. So written left to right, it's 1 7 1 3 9 7 3 9 1 0 \u2192 1,713,973,910. Yes, that's correct. So the answer is 1,713,973,910.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the sum of 734134709 and 979839201?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's add the two numbers digit by digit.  \n1. The ones place: **9 + 1 = 10** \u2192 Write **0**, carry **1**.  \n2. The tens place: **0 + 0 + 1 (carry) = 1** \u2192 Write **1**.  \n3. The hundreds place: **7 + 2 = 9** \u2192 Write **9**.  \n4. The thousands place: **4 + 9 = 13** \u2192 Write **3**, carry **1**.  \n5. The ten thousands place: **3 + 3 + 1 (carry) = 7** \u2192 Write **7**.  \n6. The hundred thousands place: **1 + 8 = 9** \u2192 Write **9**.  \n7. The millions place: **4 + 9 = 13** \u2192 Write **3**, carry **1**.  \n8. The ten millions place: **3 + 7 + 1 (carry) = 11** \u2192 Write **1**, carry **1**.  \n9. The hundred millions place: **7 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 17** \u2192 Write **7**, carry **1**.  \n10. The billions place: **1 (carry)** \u2192 Write **1**.  \n\nCombining all digits: **1,713,973,910**.  \n\nAnswer:  \nTherefore, the final computed sum is **1713973910**.",
