natively, maybe adding the numbers in parts. Let's see:\n\n142,541,887 + 129,272,940. Breaking into millions:\n\n142,541,887 is 142 million plus 541,887.\n\n129,272,940 is 129 million plus 272,940.\n\nAdding the millions: 142 + 129 = 271 million.\n\nThen adding the remaining parts: 541,887 + 272,940.\n\nCalculating that: 541,887 + 200,000 = 741,887. Then +72,940: 741,887 + 72,940 = 814,827. So total is 271,814,827. That matches the previous result. Okay, that seems right. So the answer should be 271,814,827.\n</think>\n\n",
