):4 (from 2+1+1=4?)\n\nWait, let me retrace each step carefully:\n\nStarting over:\n\nOnes place: 9 +2 =11 \u2192 1, carryover 1.\n\nTens place: 0 +0 +1 =1 \u2192 1, carryover 0.\n\nHundreds place:5 +0 =5 \u21925, carryover 0.\n\nThousands place:2 (from first number) +8 (second number) =10 \u21920, carryover 1.\n\nTen thousands place:7 +7 =14, plus carryover 1 \u219215 \u21925, carryover1.\n\nHundred thousands place:2 (first number) +1 (second number) =3, plus carryover1 \u21924 \u21924, carryover0.\n\nMillions place:4 (first) +1 (second) =5 \u21925, no carryover.\n\nTen millions place:4 (first) +1 (second) =5 \u21925, no carryover.\n\nHundred millions place:2 (first) +7 (second) =9 \u21929, no carryover.\n\nSo the digits from left to right (hundred millions down to ones):\n\n9 (hundred millions), 5 (ten millions), 5 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 5 (ten thousands), 0 (thousands), 5 (hundreds), 1 (tens), 1 (ones).\n\nSo putting that together: 955,450,511?\n\nWait, let me check that number. Let's see:\n\nBreaking down 955,450,511:\n\n- 9 hundred millions,\n\n- 5 ten millions,\n\n- 5 millions \u2192 total so far: 955,000,000\n\n- 4 hundred thousands \u2192 400,000 \u2192 955,400,000\n\n- 5 ten thousands \u219250,000 \u2192 955,450,000\n\n- 0 thousands \u2192 0 \u2192 remains 955,450,000\n\n- 5 hundreds \u2192500 \u2192 955,450,500\n\n- 1 ten \u219210 \u2192 955,450,510\n\n- 1 one \u21921 \u2192 total 955,450,511.\n\nHmm, but let me verify with another method. Maybe adding the numbers as whole:\n\n244,272,509 + 711,178,002.\n\nLet me add the millions first:\n\n244 million + 711 million = 955 million.\n\nThen the remaining parts:\n\n272,509 + 178,002.\n\n272,509 + 178,002:\n\n272,509 + 100,000 = 372,509\n\n372,509 +78,002 = 450,511.\n\nSo total is 955,000,000 + 450,511 = 955,450,511. Okay, that matches. So the answer is 955,450,511.\n\nWait, but in the initial digit-by-digit addition, the thousands place was 2 +8 =10, so we wrote 0 and carried over 1. Then the ten t