sands),4 (hundred thousands),3 (millions),2 (ten millions),1 (hundred millions). Then the carryover 1 becomes the billions place.\n\nSo the total sum would be 1 (billions) 1 (hundred millions) 2 (ten millions) 3 (millions) 4 (hundred thousands) 1 (ten thousands) 7 (thousands) 3 (hundreds) 6 (tens) 6 (ones). Wait, maybe I need to retrace.\n\nWait, let me do this step by step again carefully:\n\nLet me write both numbers with their digits separated:\n\nFirst number (417,347,196):\n\nBillions: 0 (since it's less than a billion)\nHundred millions:4\nTen millions:1\nMillions:7\nHundred thousands:3\nTen thousands:4\nThousands:7\nHundreds:1\nTens:9\nOnes:6\n\nSecond number (706,070,170):\n\nBillions:0\nHundred millions:7\nTen millions:0\nMillions:6\nHundred thousands:0\nTen thousands:7\nThousands:0\nHundreds:1\nTens:7\nOnes:0\n\nNow adding each column from right to left:\n\nOnes: 6 +0 =6\n\nTens:9 +7=16 \u2192 6, carryover 1\n\nHundreds:1 +1 +1=3 (carryover 0)\n\nThousands:7 +0=7\n\nTen thousands:4 +7=11 \u2192 1, carryover 1\n\nHundred thousands:3 +0 +1=4\n\nMillions:7 +6=13 \u21923, carryover1\n\nTen millions:1 +0 +1=2 (since the second number has 0 in ten millions)\n\nHundred millions:4 +7=11 \u21921, carryover1\n\nBillions:0 +0 +1 (carryover)=1\n\nSo putting all together from billions down:\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:6\n\nSo the number is 1,123,417,366?\n\nWait, let me check that again. Let's write the digits in order:\n\nStarting from the highest place (billions):\n\nBillions digit:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:2\n\nMillions:3\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:1\n\nThousands:7\n\nHundreds:3\n\nTens:6\n\nOnes:6\n\nSo combining these:\n\n1 (billions), 1 (hundred millions), 2 (ten millions), 3 (millions), 4 (hundred thousands), 1 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 3 (hundreds), 6 (tens), 6 (ones).\n\nSo the number is 1,123,417,366