:8+7=15 \u21925, carry1\n\nPosition8:9+5=14 +1=15 \u21925, carry1\n\nPosition9:1+9=10 +1=11 \u21921, carry1\n\nNow, after Position9, we have a carryover of 1. So the total digits are 10, with the first digit being 1 followed by the rest.\n\nSo putting all together from last to first (since we built it from right to left):\n\nThe digits from Position1 to Position9 plus the final carryover:\n\nWait, actually, the carryover after Position9 is 1, so the digits would be:\n\nCarryover 1, then the result of Position9 (1), then Position8 (5), etc. Wait, perhaps I need to list them in order.\n\nWait, let me think again. The positions are numbered from right (ones) to left (hundred millions). The carryover after the hundred millions (position9) is 1, so that becomes the next digit (billions place). So the digits from right to left are:\n\nPosition1:4\n\nPosition2:4\n\nPosition3:5\n\nPosition4:3\n\nPosition5:7\n\nPosition6:6\n\nPosition7:5\n\nPosition8:5\n\nPosition9:1\n\nPlus the final carryover 1 at the beginning (billions place).\n\nSo arranging them from left to right (billions down to ones):\n\nStarting with the carryover 1 (billions place), then the Position9 digit (1), Position8 (5), Position7 (5), Position6 (6), Position5 (7), Position4 (3), Position3 (5), Position2 (4), Position1 (4).\n\nWait, let me list them step by step:\n\nThe final digits after each position:\n\nAfter Position1: 4 (ones)\n\nAfter Position2: 4 (tens)\n\nAfter Position3:5 (hundreds)\n\nAfter Position4:3 (thousands)\n\nAfter Position5:7 (ten thousands)\n\nAfter Position6:6 (hundred thousands)\n\nAfter Position7:5 (millions)\n\nAfter Position8:5 (ten millions)\n\nAfter Position9:1 (hundred millions)\n\nPlus the carryover 1 (billions place).\n\nSo the digits from highest to lowest (billions to ones):\n\nBillions:1\n\nHundred millions:1\n\nTen millions:5\n\nMillions:5\n\nHundred thousands:6\n\nTen thousands:7\n\nThousands:3\n\nHundreds:5\n\nTens:4\n\nOnes:4\n\nWait, that might not be right. Let me stru