 it all together, starting from the right, the digits are 9 (ones), 7 (tens), 5 (hundreds), 5 (thousands), 4 (ten-thousands), 4 (hundred-thousands), 7 (millions), 6 (ten-millions), 0 (hundred-millions), 0 (billions), and the final 1 (ten-billions). So the total should be 1,058,445,579.\n\nWait, let me check again to make sure I didn't mix up any digits. Let me add them another way. Maybe breaking them into parts:\n\n689,774,096 + 368,671,483.\n\nAdding the millions first: 689,000,000 + 368,000,000 = 1,057,000,000.\n\nThen the remaining parts: 774,096 + 671,483. Let's compute that:\n\n774,096 + 600,000 = 1,374,096\n\n1,374,096 + 71,483 = 1,445,579.\n\nAdding that to the 1,057,000,000 gives 1,057,000,000 + 1,445,579 = 1,058,445,579. Okay, that matches. So the answer should be correct.\n</think>\n\n",
